        <head>HAIDOCK.</head>
        <p>HAIDOCK.</p>
        <p>4tPl'tzler Cotmcit.—The annual meeting of the ..innilic„,t_Couneil of Haydock was held on Monday. O moved that Mr. Dray ton he appointed fiot tue Council for the ensuing sear. They .40.taa„,:•!kide a better choice, and the interest and gil`ts hrssternent of the Council's business \tr would beti.,4„448. Mr. Warne secondrd, and Mr. Pilling •lilg Motion, which was carried unanimou,lv. " "PPointed vice-chairman. The Maned -;"u to the appointment of committees, .a h'ln which considerable interest was mani- "chs'ln Was appointed chairman of the ,IneleSanitary Committee, Mr.Piiiing chairman dmr. chair,:ind Gl mmitter,an i iMera Purposes Co the Gas and Water Committee. Mr. .ts r ((il Att ()Posed for the vicc-chairmanship of endance Committer, tut as it was doubt- ,- ler this the(' Was an appointment that should be tqe,.,150 s'ohneil or the committee themselves the th, tottrileferred. A long dis i ziussion took plaeo n 4itetis be !lour of meeting. It was decided that `,Q in future held at half-past three in the Thla,_,"edtha, s"3 e first Thursday in the inonth. It was 'quay ill committee meetings be held en the last 6,6rY month.</p>
